E. SYNTHESIS: WHAT TOURNAMENT ANALYSIS IS TESTING
======================================================================================================================
  abstraction stack:
    raw data -> metric/sensor -> comparator -> tournament -> invariants -> wall-crossing path

  Score lifts are rankers.  They orient i,j by scalar s_i - s_j, so distinct scores force transitive tournaments.
    observed score transitive samples: 316/316
  Edge-local and edge-switch lifts are analyzers.  They decide every pair from pair- or lens-specific data, so cycles can survive.
    observed edge-local transitive samples: 1/290

  useful layer names:
    flux lift:       directed counts, e.g. basketball passes i->j vs j->i
    phase lift:      circular half-turn/chirality from moving runners
    rank lift:       any centrality, distance-to-anchor, entropy, or isolation score
    lens lift:       pair i,j compared through a third label, anchor, or shifted coordinate
    switch lift:     symmetric distance D_ij toggles a base Hamiltonian-path edge
    volume lift:     oriented area/volume after embedding in sphere/cuboid/simplex
    dynamic lift:    edge flips as the continuous variable crosses comparator walls

  repo connection: the Hamiltonian tie-break path is not a detail.  It is the fixed labelled path used to complete ties, just as the tiling model uses a base path and S22 used lex completion for degenerate circle states.
